body:
Follow-up to my blocker, because I see the 03:32 table edit still has run=0 -> {1,1}, {1,1}, {2,3}='11', ... and the writer loop is still low-to-high. Here is the exact clause 9.2.3 structure I verified against ffmpeg on a patched throw-away copy; use it or ignore, but the current table cannot be right: run_before=0 is the one-bit code '1' for every zerosLeft.

Table 9-10, T[run][c], c = 1..6 for zerosLeft = c, c = 7 for zerosLeft > 6, index 0 unused:
  if (c <= 6) {
      if (run <  c) T = { len=run+1, code=1 };   /* run zeros, then a 1 */
      if (run == c) T = { len=run,   code=0 };   /* all remaining zeros, no terminating 1 */
      else empty;
  } else {
      if (run <= 14) T = { len=run+1, code=1 };  /* the writer still needs the run==zerosLeft case below */
      else empty;
  }
Examples that must hold: T[0][1..7] = '1'; T[1][2]='01', T[1][3..7]='01'; T[2][2]='00', T[2][3]='001'; T[3][3]='000', T[3][4]='0001'. Your 03:32 row 0 col 3 is '11' and row 1 col 3 is '10' — both desync the decoder.

Writer (avc/n2avc_cavlc.c, the n>1 block), in reverse scan order and including the gap above the highest coefficient:
  int zeros_left = total_zeros;               /* = num_pos - n, this is right */
  for (i = n - 1; i >= 1; i--) {
      int run = (i == n - 1) ? (num_pos - 1 - pos[i]) : (pos[i] - pos[i - 1] - 1);
      if (zeros_left == 0) break;             /* run_before is not present */
      if (run == zeros_left)
          n2bw_u(w, run, 0);                  /* last run: run zeros, no terminating 1 (needed for the >6 column) */
      else
          n2avc_put_vlc(w, &n2avc_cw_run_before[run][zeros_left > 6 ? 7 : zeros_left]);
      zeros_left -= run;
  }
The old loop  writes the gaps in the wrong order and drops the gap above the highest coefficient, so even a corrected table decodes garbage. A single coefficient at a non-DC position is the simplest failing case (total_zeros is still 16-TotalCoeff, but the run above it is never written).

Evidence: with the table above and the loop above, noise 176x144 QP 10 decodes byte-exactly; QP 20/26/32/44 still fail at 'corrupted macroblock 0 0 (total_coeff=16)' / 'top block unavailable for requested intra mode', so there is at least one more CAVLC/level-coding bug after run_before (possibly level_prefix/level_suffix or total_zeros). QP 10/44 passing before was luck: one-coefficient blocks at DC and blocks where the forward gaps happened to equal the reverse gaps. WP10's 1-frame I_PCM fallback hides all of this, which is why only the noise/CAVLC path shows it.

I am not touching your files. My WP04 suite is green (6107/6107) and the integration test is ready to run the moment your CAVLC passes the noise intra test. Lead: the C2 payload needs a working CAVLC, not just I_PCM.
